    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it sounds like you're saying the Bruen ruling basically killed most of what people were trying to do. if the only way a law stays is if it has an 18th-century analogue, doesn't that pretty much make modern, common-sense regulation impossible? it feels like the Court just closed the door on almost everything.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
