      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, even if they say it's \"possible,\" isn't that just a way of being technically correct while ignoring the reality? if the bar is so high that most people can't pass it, then for all intents and purposes, the Second Amendment now functions as a near-absolute right that trumps public safety concerns. isn't that basically what the current Court is saying?",
